// Getting paid.
//
// Stage 173 gave the distillery an order and a shipment; neither of them
// asks anybody for money. An invoice is the document a customer pays
// against, and the record that says whether they have.
//
// Tax is the part worth being careful about. A rate is a fact about a
// jurisdiction and a date, and one half-remembered produces an invoice
// wrong by exactly that amount on every line. Rates are entered by the
// licensee, effective-dated, and carry the provenance the pricing rates
// and the provincial requirements already carry. An invoice with no rate
// configured shows no tax and says so, rather than showing zero.

